# Example upssched.conf for RP-node2 (see CLAUDE.md topology).
#
# Install at /etc/nut/upssched.conf and adjust the CMDSCRIPT path to the
# real deploy path (CLAUDE.md: /home/pi/Projects/homelab-energy). This is a
# template only: nothing here is applied automatically, and it is not a
# substitute for upsmon.conf already having
#   NOTIFYCMD /usr/bin/upssched-cmd
# (path confirmed on RP-node2's Debian/Raspbian packaging — check yours
# with `which upssched-cmd`, it varies by distro) and NOTIFYFLAG entries
# with the EXEC bit for the events below, e.g.:
#   NOTIFYFLAG ONLINE  SYSLOG+EXEC
#   NOTIFYFLAG ONBATT  SYSLOG+EXEC
#   NOTIFYFLAG LOWBATT SYSLOG+EXEC
#
# upsmon runs upssched-cmd as its own notify user (e.g. "nut", split from
# the root process that does the actual shutdown), not whoever owns this
# checkout. bin/homelab-energy-cmdscript pins STATE_DIR to
# /var/lib/homelab-energy for that reason — see docs/runbook.md's
# pre-test checklist for creating that directory with the right owner.

CMDSCRIPT /home/pi/Projects/homelab-energy/bin/homelab-energy-cmdscript

AT ONBATT * EXECUTE ONBATT
AT ONLINE * EXECUTE ONLINE
AT LOWBATT * EXECUTE LOWBATT
